{
  "id": "object-and-methods-5-the-math-class",
  "moduleId": "object-and-methods",
  "title": "The Math class",
  "order": 6,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "**The predefined `Math` class provides a number of standard mathematical methods. No import statement is required.**"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Lesson 10 covered these in detail. One method not shown there:"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [
        "Name",
        "Description",
        "Argument type",
        "Return type",
        "Example",
        "Value returned"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "`pow`",
          "Power",
          "`double`",
          "`double`",
          "`Math.pow(2.0, 3.0)`",
          "`8.0`"
        ],
        [
          "`abs`",
          "Absolute value",
          "`int`, `long`, `float`, `double`",
          "same as argument",
          "`Math.abs(-7)`<br>`Math.abs(-3.5)`",
          "`7`<br>`3.5`"
        ],
        [
          "`max`",
          "Maximum",
          "`int`, `long`, `float`, `double`",
          "same as argument",
          "`Math.max(5, 6)`<br>`Math.max(5.5, 5.3)`",
          "`6`<br>`5.5`"
        ],
        [
          "`min`",
          "Minimum",
          "`int`, `long`, `float`, `double`",
          "same as argument",
          "`Math.min(5, 6)`",
          "`5`"
        ],
        [
          "`random`",
          "Random number",
          "none",
          "`double`",
          "`Math.random()`",
          "a number ≥ 0.0 and < 1.0"
        ],
        [
          "`round`",
          "Rounding",
          "`float` or `double`",
          "`int` or `long` respectively",
          "`Math.round(6.2)`<br>`Math.round(6.8)`",
          "`6`<br>`7`"
        ],
        [
          "`ceil`",
          "Ceiling",
          "`double`",
          "`double`",
          "`Math.ceil(3.2)`",
          "`4.0`"
        ],
        [
          "`floor`",
          "Floor",
          "`double`",
          "`double`",
          "`Math.floor(3.9)`",
          "`3.0`"
        ],
        [
          "`sqrt`",
          "Square root",
          "`double`",
          "`double`",
          "`Math.sqrt(4.0)`",
          "`2.0`"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "variant": "correction",
      "title": "Correction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "your handout describes `Math.random()` as returning a number \"**>0** and <1.\" The lower bound is **inclusive**: it can return exactly `0.0`, though never `1.0`. The range is `[0.0, 1.0)`."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "value": "Using Math.random"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "The raw value is rarely what you want. The standard formula for a whole number in a range:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "value": "(int) (Math.random() * (max - min + 1)) + min"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "value": "public class DiceRoller {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        for (int i = 1; i <= 5; i++) {\n            int roll = (int) (Math.random() * 6) + 1;   // 1 to 6\n            System.out.println(\"Roll \" + i + \": \" + roll);\n        }\n\n        int percent = (int) (Math.random() * 101);      // 0 to 100\n        System.out.println(\"Random percent: \" + percent);\n    }\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Trace the dice line: `Math.random()` gives `[0.0, 1.0)`, times 6 gives `[0.0, 6.0)`, cast to `int` truncates to `0`–`5`, plus 1 gives `1`–`6`. The `+ 1` is **outside** the cast: inside it, you would round the wrong thing."
    }
  ]
}
